**[P3]** Could `parseOptOutInstant` accept lowercase `T`/`Z` and truncate digits past nanoseconds, as Android, iOS and the edge do? I know a96b572 chose rejection over truncation on purpose. The case for reconsidering is consistency: since a96b572, JS is the only one of the three SDKs that rejects these values.

I ran the same 18 strings through this parser at 3704387, through the Android and iOS parsers from DataDog/dd-sdk-android#4024 and DataDog/dd-sdk-ios#3338 (their code, copied verbatim), and through chrono 0.4.45, which the edge in ddoghq/dd-source#140422 locks.
